WEBVTT

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:36.240
"Graduation"

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.870
Captain Simon, congratulations
on successfully

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:48.270
destroying the enemy base on RA221.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:51.750
Indeed, that was splendid!

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.460
We finally managed to land a blow
against the Wulgaru army.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.090
There's hope yet that we can change
the tide of this war.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.100
The real battle has yet to begin.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.510
Until now, the Wulgaru
has taken us lightly,

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:06.640
but that strike will serve as an excuse
to launch a massive attack.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.740
Precisely.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.920
We must prepare for the
Wulgaru's counter-attack.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.650
We have already confirmed signs
of enemy movement.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.650
You are speaking out
of line, Deputy Amane.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.150
My apologies.

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:22.200
But after this, I imagine
the MJP will be back

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.810
on track, training pilots.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.770
If they pump out more
excellent students,

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.830
we might actually win this war!

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:29.880
Yes, indeed!

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:32.070
We need to increase the AHSMB
unit's production speed.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:49.600
Yo!

00:02:52.310 --> 00:02:55.530
See, that was a pretty
hard fight back there,

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.300
so maintenance has been killer.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.570
Our Rhinos are just prototypes
for your AHSMBs.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.740
But the way you fought with them...!

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.280
You guys should be able
to show us up easy.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.620
You've just gotta get a
grasp on your units first.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:16.820
Our DNA has been programmed
into our units,

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.450
which makes piloting them relatively easy.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.630
But don't rely too heavily on
your machine's abilities.

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:26.060
If one side relies too heavily on the other,
the relationship is screwed.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.920
So, did ya need somethin'?

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:32.350
I don't have any porn on hand
if that's what ya want.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:33.420
Uh, no!

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:36.860
We received orders to return
to the academy again.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.590
I just wanted to say "Goodbye" first.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.190
That right?

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.200
Well, I'm sure we'll run into
each other again someday.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.610
After all, the enemy
is already on the move.

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.590
Oh, right! Before I forget.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:02.980
This contains the data
from our last battle.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.470
I had it stored on my Rhinos.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:09.630
One of our duties is to collect combat data
for future generations.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.480
Thank you.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:16.170
Hang in there!

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:20.360
After this, we'll be headin'
back to the frontlines.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:20.900
See ya 'round.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.440
Right!

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:46.640
Data from the Rhinos units, huh?

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:49.930
As far as the bigwigs are concerned,
all of us are just data.

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:56.020
Where is Doberman going next?

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.670
Back to the frontlines.

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.100
Is that right?

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.540
We'll see them again.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.300
Huh? What're you doing here?

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.720
Why the heck did you come back?

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:29.890
Well, we're not sure why ourselves.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:32.920
You're still lacking where it counts.

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:34.660
That's what makes you the Fail Five!

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:37.670
That last strike only worked because

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.810
those other pilots were there, huh?

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:45.650
Just try not to make the
rest of us look bad.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:49.160
Asagi!

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.420
This place never changes!

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.420
Yep. It's kinda relaxing.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.750
That isn't relaxing!

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.310
And here we're working our butts off!

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:05.550
Seriously!

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.470
Ah, sirs!

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.180
Instructor Suzukaze is calling for you.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:14.720
Oh, thank you.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:16.310
It was nothing.

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:19.560
Now if you'll pardon me, Team Fail.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.400
Team Fail?

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.490
Did she do that on purpose?

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.310
She seriously thought
that was our team name...

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:34.410
Huh?

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.850
What does graduating entail?

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:39.860
In short, it means you have
completed your training

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:42.790
and will officially enter the GDF army.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.010
The five of you will
be graduating early.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:50.470
Likewise, I will be
transferring with you.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.150
I will be the captain of the Godinion:
your superior commander.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:01.150
Pack your belongings in your dorm rooms.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.920
You will return to Star Rose tomorrow

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.860
and remain on standby
until tomorrow's mission.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.480
Understood?

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:22.040
What Life Brought You

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.720
Now they're rushing
us through graduation?

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.570
Guess that means, "From now on,

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:38.820
we can throw you into as many
battles as we want!" huh?

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.090
Aren't you going to miss this place?

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:47.980
I never dreamed I'd feel this way
when I first came here...

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.530
We were practically
thrown into the school.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.600
Boy was I shocked when I found out
we were on the same team...

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:24.520
Now for the next team.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.260
Toshikazu Asagi,

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:27.740
Ataru Suruga,

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.150
Izuru Hitachi,

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:30.530
Kei Kugimiya,

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:31.790
and Tamaki Irie.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:33.610
Ma'am...

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.660
Yes?

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.620
Everyone is younger than me...

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:37.920
Is that a problem?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.290
So if you have any questions,
please feel free to ask.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:56.640
Come to think of it, Suruga,
didn't you start out pretty quiet?

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.060
I had no idea what to talk about!

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.810
Our memories had just been wiped.

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:03.180
True enough.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.980
Aside from class and the weather,
there was nothing to talk about.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.730
Whoo, class!

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:14.240
Team Rabbits, you have excellent
offensive capabilities and mobility,

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:18.280
but you're getting E's in cooperation,
concentration and operational stability!

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.160
Cooperation is an outright E-!

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.380
That'd give her a fairly
large cup size...

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.500
What are you talking about?

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.920
An F would have been even better yet.

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.080
E is the lowest grade you can get!

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:31.500
Uh, guys...!

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:43.640
For some odd reason, everyone
started to open up after that.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:44.640
All thanks to me, huh?

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:45.980
Not quite...

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:47.460
Keep out of this.

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:56.150
Doesn't it feel empty now?

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.170
Yeah...

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.490
Could I take this with me?

00:10:04.210 --> 00:10:06.870
Sure, didn't it belong to whoever
stayed here before us?

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.260
It's a tattered mess, anyway.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.000
It's the first manga I ever read.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:15.920
NEW
SERIALIZATION!
BUDDY SPIRITS 3

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.800
Well, this is a load off.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:22.600
It's nice knowing that we don't have
to come back here anymore.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:23.850
Sure is!

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:27.730
I bet no one dreamed we'd be piloting
the high-tech AHSMB units

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:29.520
and graduating ahead of everyone else.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.650
Not in their wildest dreams!

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:35.070
Hey, where are you going?

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:35.980
Gonna cry?

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.660
You're gonna cry by yourself, aren't ya?

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.070
I want to draw one last sketch.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:56.800
FAIL

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:55.790
In the end, I never could
get this to come off...

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:10.640
What are you doing here?

00:11:10.890 --> 00:11:12.310
Right back at you, Kei!

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:15.320
We came to clean out our desks.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.650
How to Get a Wonderful Girlfriend
Learn how girls think!
Ways for 'meh' guys
to find romance!

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.700
That's a magazine for guys.

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.370
DANCING CAKES
Make dough for popular cakes,
simple baked sweets that make your mouth dance,
and French recipes you've always dreamt of.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:27.370
Ladies, what were you
two doing during class?

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.790
You're not one to talk!

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:33.600
No wonder we were called the Fail Five.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.840
It's seriously no wonder at all, huh?

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:58.480
So this is where you went!

00:11:58.860 --> 00:11:59.860
What are you up to?

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.400
Uh, nothing...

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.780
Asagi was wanting to fly one last lap
around the campus.

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:04.780
I never said that!

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.410
Your AHSMBs are currently being
transported to the school.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.230
Lieutenant Amane.

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:36.560
First Lt. Shirato.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:37.820
Is something the matter?

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:41.320
Not really. The meeting just ended.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.240
All of the economic powers

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:47.420
are squabbling over the
AHSMB technology and units.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:51.450
After fighting a losing war for so long,
we had our first victory.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:55.670
It's only natural for the MJP
and the AHSMBs to garner attention.

00:12:55.670 --> 00:13:00.420
But they don't care about
fighting the enemy!

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:03.590
Each country merely wants to
stand above the others.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:06.530
Fighting the Wulgaru isn't easy,

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:09.270
but Earth politics are no
laughing matter either.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.560
They're so desperate for the technology

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:14.270
that some are asking to sponsor
Gurantseere Cosmopolitan Academy.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.650
Others are trying to
volunteer new students.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:18.730
Doesn't this fall outside
of your jurisdiction?

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:21.320
Yes, but with Commander Simon away...

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:22.500
Is he visiting the academy?

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:31.830
Are they ready?

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:36.210
Sir! They are already packed.
I believe they could leave tomorrow.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:37.460
Very well.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.050
I believe it is still too soon for them

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.860
to become official members of the army...

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:44.840
Your reasoning?

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:48.730
They have not fully
mastered their AHSMBs...

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:52.160
Plus they still seem uncertain
about the JURIA-SYSTEM.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.900
Due to their innate personalities,

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:57.440
Tamaki Irie and Ataru
Suruga are adjusting to

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:58.790
the SYSTEM relatively well.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.820
However, Asagi and Kugimiya both

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:05.530
deteriorate and freeze on the battlefield.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:11.270
At times, Izuru Hitachi displays
bursts of power, but not reliably.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:14.790
But there is nothing left
for you to teach them here.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:19.280
I imagine the JURIA-SYSTEM
can only be mastered on the battlefield.

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:23.960
It requires situations where they
put their very lives on the line.

00:14:26.630 --> 00:14:28.330
I will see to tomorrow's preparations.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:42.730
What are those?

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:43.570
AHSMB?!

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:45.280
Awesome! Are they real?

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:47.400
They're nothing like our practice units.

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:55.410
Why the heck do we have to do
a demonstration?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:56.540
Don't ask me!

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:58.370
Good morning.

00:14:58.370 --> 00:14:59.460
You're here early.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:01.920
This is just a demonstration.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.000
It's hardly something
to stress out over.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:07.010
We're stressed BECAUSE
it's a demonstration.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.170
It could be scarier than a real battle.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:11.270
Do we seriously have to
go through with this?

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.520
As I explained yesterday,

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.880
Blue 1 and Red 5 will perform linkages.

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:20.190
Gold 4 will fire while under 1G.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.270
You'll be using live ammo,

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.380
so bear in mind the
gravity, wind, humidity

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.610
and air density while calculating your trajectory.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:30.530
Purple 2 will issue orders and Rose 3
will offer aerial support.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.490
That comprises this demonstration.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:34.580
The one thing I suck at...

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:37.620
You failed once in front of
the entire universe, remember?

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:38.450
Shut it!

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.850
At least you get to show off!

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:42.250
All I get to do is shoot!

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:42.880
Don't tell me...

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:44.740
I'm issuing orders from THERE?

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:46.880
You're on stage!

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.410
That might be the most
embarrassing job...

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:06.400
Team Rabbits will hereby offer you
a demonstration.

00:16:08.730 --> 00:16:11.530
I never expected a mission like this
before graduation...

00:16:11.990 --> 00:16:13.070
Let's do our best!

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.910
This is a great chance to rid ourselves
of the name "Fail Five".

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:19.540
Dude, you're planning to become
an instant school hero, aren't you?

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.630
This really is a great
opportunity, isn't it?

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:23.250
Assuming we don't fail!

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:40.430
Blue 1, Gold 4, Red 5, take off!

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:56.700
Blue 1, Red 5, linkage!

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.300
Rose 3, blast off!

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:58.220
Tamaki, you went lower
than you were supposed to...

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:04.140
Gold 4, now!

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:15.940
No one was watching me!

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:17.830
Who was that applause for?!

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:26.640
That is all for their demonstration.

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:44.430
It's over...

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:46.130
I'm beat!

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:51.610
Hey!

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.740
Sorry for everything.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:58.490
It won't be the same without you guys.

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:01.200
Although we'll be hitting
the frontlines soon enough.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:05.370
Bye! Let's meet up again
sometime, Fail Five!

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:06.790
Of all the nerve!

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:18.880
Graduates, enter.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:33.810
Come receive your medal
of rank, Tamaki Irie.

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:34.980
Ma'am!

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:41.570
Kei Kugimiya.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.080
Toshikazu Asagi.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:46.830
Ma'am!

00:19:58.590 --> 00:19:59.700
Are you all right?

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:05.000
What a doozy...

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:11.290
What were you thinking, Asagi?

00:20:11.290 --> 00:20:12.350
I'll regret it forever.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:15.150
I bet that gave you three
holes in your tummy.

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.020
Did you get hurt?

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:18.510
Nah, I'm fine.

00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:22.150
Asagi hogged all of the attention
back there, didn't he?

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:24.270
That's not the type of attention I want!

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:28.680
Hurry on!

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:35.500
We'll never come back
here again, will we?

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:36.630
Yeah...

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:39.270
That's kinda... sad.

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:43.970
From now on...

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:48.400
Wherever our team is,
that will be where our home is.

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:51.890
Let's strive...

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:54.060
...to do our best as Team Fail!

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.730
That's not our team name!

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:56.480
Really?

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.110
Don't gimme that!

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:00.710
Stoopy-poopy-doopy head!

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:11.000
Look!

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:55.950
"Stronghold of Lust"
